BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 608.10 Tm (hosts that did run but ran slow: the same operator rented a 4090 that drew 350 watts when a stock 4090 is 450, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 592.87 Tm (listing disk speeds ranged from about 180 megabytes a second to over 30,000 [kvP__Lh53oM @ 00:00:53]. Old) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 577.65 Tm (machines behind cheap cards are the second trap, with 3060s often sitting on retired mining rigs with 2016-era CPUs) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 562.42 Tm (where the host hands over 16 of 64 cores, so jobs load forever and then fail to compile [dWC3n2Bn3r8 @ 00:03:06].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 547.20 Tm (Newer cards are not immune: every 5060 GPU Battle tried to rent came back underclocked, saddled with a crappy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 531.97 Tm (CPU, or short on RAM, making it useless for testing [WhTJ6B-YCmw @ 00:07:40]. The economics check is blunt:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 516.75 Tm (duds cost pennies, slow hosts cost real money, and one bad host can wipe out the whole discount.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 501.52 Tm (Interruptible capacity is where cheap turns into lost work. GPU Battle bid on Vast spot pods 17 times and eight got) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 486.30 Tm (kicked off before they finished, about half, which the operator rates great for a quick test and terrible for anything you) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 471.07 Tm (cannot restart [kvP__Lh53oM @ 00:01:13]. Bryan Software describes the nightmare version: a training run spins up,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 455.85 Tm (runs 40 minutes, the host drops, and you lose both the compute time and the checkpoint, with Vast's provisioning score) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 440.62 Tm (at 3.6 out of five and no platform-wide contractual SLA [Ez2jsa33jFY @ 00:02:38]. Worse, the same operator flags) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 425.40 Tm (that Vast's interruptible tier bills the license cost even on interrupted hours, so the 10 to 30% interruption loss is a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 410.17 Tm (charge already paid, not a refund, and an unsaved checkpoint means paying for compute you cannot recover) Tj ET
