BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 379.72 Tm (and a safety buffer to the offer's maximum rental window, because a cheap offer that expires before the checkpoint) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 364.50 Tm (finishes is just a very affordable way to fail, and if one retry ruins the deadline, the lowest row may become the most) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 349.27 Tm (expensive decision [cEAhnKuawL8 @ 00:01:02]. The rule that falls out: spot is for restartable work only, and anything) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 334.05 Tm (with a deadline needs a host that can finish.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 318.82 Tm (The quietest bleed is the bill that keeps running after the work stops. HostingCompared with Natalie spells out that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 303.60 Tm (stopping a RunPod pod releases the GPU but the volume disk keeps billing at the stopped rate of 20 cents per gigabyte) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 288.37 Tm (per month, so 100 gigabytes is $20 a month, while on Vast storage keeps billing while the machine is online until you) Tj ET
