BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 493.77 Tm (The most expensive trap is cheap spot capacity run without discipline. The Code Notebook simulated a 100-hour job) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 478.55 Tm (with interruptions every eight hours, a six-minute restart, 72 seconds per save, 2,000 runs, and a 70% discount: never) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 463.32 Tm (saving stretched the job to 2,203,564 hours, saving every 30 minutes finished in 109 hours at a cost of 32.6 against 100) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 448.10 Tm (on-demand, and saving every 30 seconds ballooned to 345 hours at 103.5 [IZtzUfhm8LU @ 00:09:58]. Their verdict is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 432.87 Tm (that spot without checkpoints is not cheap, saving too often costs more than not using spot at all, and the optimal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 417.65 Tm (interval is the square root of two times mean time between interruptions times save cost, about 34 minutes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 402.42 Tm ([IZtzUfhm8LU @ 00:10:20]. The same speaker notes the warning windows are brutal: AWS gives two minutes and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 387.20 Tm (Azure gives 30 seconds. Codemia's scheduler design polls the two-minute reclaim notice every five seconds and tells) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 371.97 Tm (operators to give each job a random offset so checkpoint timers do not line up, because correlated failures are where) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 356.75 Tm (these systems break [a_zou7QahAo @ 00:31:58]. SkyPilot's managed jobs layer pitches hands-free recovery from GPU) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 341.52 Tm (failure, node maintenance, quota reclamation, and spot preemption so nobody gets paged at 3:00 a.m. [uwLkrJb5pEA) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 326.30 Tm (@ 00:08:31].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 311.07 Tm (The second trap is paying for GPUs that are not doing work. The gpuMaster's core warning is that stalled GPUs still) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 295.85 Tm (bill, and that large-scale GPU workloads are far less forgiving [_tV0Elv_jIk @ 00:01:29]. Caleb Writes Code measured) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 280.62 Tm (the scaling tax: efficiency drops to 77% at eight GPUs under model parallelism and 74% at 512, and fragmented nodes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 265.40 Tm (turn scheduling into Tetris [9u2hCf8FlW0 @ 00:05:04]. Seung Jin Yang of SkyPilot debugged the failures researchers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 250.17 Tm (actually hit when they ask why their job is not scheduled: fragmentation, rogue taints left by agents, a request for 128) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 234.95 Tm (CPUs on nodes with only about 126.32 allocatable that shows up as blocked, and quota oversubscription where 12) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 219.72 Tm (GPUs are promised against 8, which, in their words, can happen in practice [tb-Yg8PNXT4 @ 00:13:27]. Codemia) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 204.50 Tm (prices the gap: default Kubernetes gets about 45% utilization, a workload-aware design about 85%, a spread worth) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 189.27 Tm (roughly $150,000 per day on a 10,000-GPU fleet [a_zou7QahAo @ 00:04:38]. The same speaker caps defragmentation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 174.05 Tm (at 5% per hour, because the cure has to stay cheaper than the disease. Every one of these leaks lands as billed GPU) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 158.82 Tm (hours with zero training progress behind them.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 143.60 Tm (The third trap is the balance sheet. Tulipnomics walks through the telecom bust as a template: Lucent promised $6.7) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 128.37 Tm (billion in customer credit by September 2000, with Nortel and Cisco running similar programs, summed up as the seller) Tj ET
