BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (node without a card, so mixed clusters stay clean [f-FKoMHqRoI @ 00:00:35]. Saiyam of vCluster lists the full) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (payload the operator drops onto each GPU node: CUDA drivers, the container runtime, the device plugin, metrics, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (GPU feature discovery [sXpJ4vSc-cM @ 00:31:46]. That discovery layer is what surfaces sharing to the Kubernetes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (scheduler. On Rafay's MKS cluster, the operator stamps nvidia.com labels onto the GPU node reporting GPU present) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (true, an NVIDIA A10, a physical count of 1, and a time-slicing strategy with 10 replicas, so a single card shows up to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (the scheduler as ten [n-O8p7y9Z5A @ 00:00:44]. Jitesh Powankar calls enablement straightforward: install the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (operator, configure node policies, and once configured Kubernetes automatically discovers the new slices and reports) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (them like CPU or memory [Ul1dZowvKvE @ 00:03:58]. The operator consensus is that nobody hand-rolls drivers and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (device plugins per node; the operator owns that layer, and every sharing strategy - time slicing, MIG, or fractional) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (scheduling - is expressed as a label, a config, or an annotation that the operator and scheduler reconcile.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (The business case is idle silicon. Jitesh Powankar puts numbers on it: a pod that requests a whole card may use only 20) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (to 30 percent, leaving 70 percent idle while other pods queue - like booking a whole 50-seat bus for one passenger) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm ([Ul1dZowvKvE @ 00:00:34]. The Code Architect drills into the hardware reason: a light task occupies about 10) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (percent of the streaming multiprocessors and the other 90 percent sit idle, because separate CUDA contexts cannot run) Tj ET
