BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 261.55 Tm (Body: Four field-tested adjustments the practitioners applied once the basic operator install was running.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 246.32 Tm (Items: Match vLLM's GPU memory utilization to the Ray placement fraction, because a 0.25 GPU request on its own) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 231.10 Tm (can still saturate 100 percent of the device and let PyTorch and vLLM each grab the whole VRAM [The Code) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 215.87 Tm (Architect - TwICQ_zP8Ys @ 00:07:14].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 200.65 Tm (Do not trust nvidia-smi on time-sliced cards: on a 24 GB L4 with 5 replicas it showed 13 GB while the pod's real usage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 185.42 Tm (was 4 GB [CNCF - Vw7DTM1SV60 @ 00:04:56].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 170.20 Tm (Inside each tenant vCluster, reinstall the GPU operator with the toolkit and driver disabled, reapply and re-patch time) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 154.97 Tm (slicing, and refresh the node if the 4 replicas do not show [vCluster - KzJvhbdgvl8 @ 00:02:09].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 139.75 Tm (Set NVIDIA_DRIVER_CAPABILITIES to compute and utility when the model does not use video, keep the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 124.53 Tm (nvidia.com/gpu limit explicit, and add a toleration keyed nvidia.com/gpu to clear the GPU node's NoSchedule taint) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 109.30 Tm ([DevOps & AI Toolkit - zuRKdveFuZ4 @ 00:07:02].) Tj ET
