BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 301.77 Tm (Memory is where shared GPUs die first. Julien Semaan's Kubex demo put 5 time-slice replicas on a 24 GB L4, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 286.55 Tm (nvidia-smi showed 13 GB for a pod whose real usage was 4 GB, so the standard tool misreported who was actually) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 271.32 Tm (eating the card [Vw7DTM1SV60 @ 00:04:56]. Then a leaky classifier on the same GPU pushed LLM A into OOM,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 256.10 Tm (killing the well-behaved tenant instead of the offender. The Code Architect traces the same failure to layer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 240.87 Tm (misalignment: when hardware, driver and orchestration layers disagree, the result is OOM errors and node crashes, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 225.65 Tm (Ray's fractional request only sets CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES, letting PyTorch and vLLM each grab the whole) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 210.42 Tm (VRAM [TwICQ_zP8Ys @ 00:01:14]. Yuan Chen's GPU-burn benchmark quantified the imbalance: under plain time) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 195.20 Tm (slicing, job 1 took about ten times job 2's memory, and only MPS with 50% limits evened it out [nOgxv_R13Dg @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 179.97 Tm (00:23:49]. Dynamia.ai's HAMi talk adds the utilization cost: without memory isolation, OOM crashes tanked) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 164.75 Tm (utilization, and reserved memory, 5 GB in their example, is not the same thing as consumed memory, so unused) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 149.52 Tm (reservations and noisy neighbors both have to be watched [zrGFmLHI7hg @ 00:09:22]. The economics check is blunt:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 134.30 Tm (an unenforced fraction is an outage waiting for the noisiest neighbor on the card, and it takes down the paying tenant) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 119.07 Tm (first.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 103.85 Tm (The second trap is capacity that exists on paper but never schedules. Jitesh Powankar frames the baseline waste: a pod) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 88.62 Tm (requesting a whole card may use only 20 to 30 percent, leaving 70 percent idle while other pods queue, like booking a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 73.40 Tm (whole 50-seat bus for one passenger [Ul1dZowvKvE @ 00:00:34]. DevOps & AI Toolkit hit it live on GKE: after) Tj ET
