BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 313.15 Tm (each block hash chains to the previous one, so arbitrary substrings never match, while SGLang runs a token-level radix) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 297.92 Tm (tree with LRU eviction and schedules requests with the most cached tokens first; semantic similarity does not count,) Tj ET
