BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.55 Tm (The gateway layer fails in quiet, billable ways. Ready Tensor set a $500 budget on a LiteLLM virtual key and watched) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.32 Tm (the request that crossed the line still succeed. Only the next call returned a 400 'budget exceeded' error plus a Slack) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.10 Tm (alert, so the overshoot lands on you [9t-W51EHgzY @ 00:12:43]. Jono Finds lists the self-hosted proxy's operational) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.87 Tm (debt. Import time runs 3-4 seconds, which hurts serverless. The database degrades after 1M entries, and at 100,000) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.65 Tm (requests a day that threshold arrives in 10 days. The dashboard dies when you disable logging. A September 2025) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.42 Tm (release caused memory failures, and a founder advised avoiding it [XZPNjgJ4E0c @ 00:04:07]. On the managed side,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.20 Tm (Jono Finds flags credits that expire after a year, failed free-tier requests that still count against the limit, and agentic) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 380.97 Tm (workflows that produce surprise bills [XZPNjgJ4E0c @ 00:02:24]. Mariselle Hartwell's sharpest warning is about) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 365.75 Tm (security. Hartwell cites a credential-harvesting compromise and says that self-hosting the open-source router means) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 350.52 Tm (you own the attack surface, including the database, caching and patching [pa2rbXDnUYM @ 00:01:57].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 335.30 Tm (Cheap hardware breaks at the slowest link. Cian Mag added a fourth laptop to the llama.cpp RPC cluster and got slower) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 320.07 Tm (output than with three, because 2.5GbE moves only about 312 MB/s. In Cian Mag's words: 'Otherwise, you're adding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 304.85 Tm (another machine that the rest of the cluster has to wait for' [kgSARM9iGF4 @ 00:07:10]. Cian Mag also calls the RPC) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 289.62 Tm (backend fragile and insecure, keeps it off open networks, and admits to having no verified power or cost data) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 274.40 Tm ([kgSARM9iGF4 @ 00:08:36]. Byte Forensics attacks the NVMe-offload pitch directly. Fitting a model is not the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 259.17 Tm (as running it efficiently, mmap and the page cache are not VRAM, and heavy swapping makes the workload) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 243.95 Tm (unresponsive [ux5n4VAhUNU @ 00:02:52]. Remy Runs confirms the bandwidth math on a live rig. A 3090 has) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 228.72 Tm (roughly 4.5x the bandwidth of 8-channel DDR4, and Optane reads around 8 GB/s and is about 3x slower on random) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 213.50 Tm (reads. A 32K-token prefill took over a minute, stretching to about 2.5 minutes over Thunderbolt [o6WzuMA5VL8 @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 198.27 Tm (00:12:04]. Remy also found that a single flag, -cpu-moe, was the difference between under 1 and about 10 tok/s on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 183.05 Tm (GPT-OSS 120B. Supply is turning against the build too: Optane is end-of-life, and DRAM contract prices rose about) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 167.82 Tm (90% in a quarter.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 152.60 Tm (Free and cheap endpoints collapse under agent traffic. Bruno Vega's Kaggle server faces GPU queues over 15 minutes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 137.37 Tm (and a 32K context cap. Agent harnesses send 8-30K tokens up front, about 85 seconds of prefill, while the Cloudflare) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 122.15 Tm (tunnel cuts requests at 100 seconds [KVXaHQu32Rw @ 00:12:40]. Tooling mattered: the same edit task took 29.5s) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 106.92 Tm (through the pi harness versus 92.7s through open code. Kaggle's AUP also lists server farming as abuse, so multiple) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 91.70 Tm (accounts are out, and prompts pass through Google and Cloudflare [KVXaHQu32Rw @ 00:16:09]. Bruno's own value) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 76.47 Tm (math is blunt: 3.24M tokens a week is worth about $1.50 at $0.15/$0.47 per million. Daniel at Data Science Festival) Tj ET
