BT /F2 8 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 755.00 Tm (THE BIG MONEY PLAYBOOKS) Tj ET
0.6 w 54.00 747.00 m 558.00 747.00 l S
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (Tony Lewis lays out the self-signing bill line by line. The iconectiv token runs thousands a year, priced as a percentage) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (of 499 revenue with a minimum fee, getting it means clearing a multi-page sandbox test case, and the certificate itself) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (costs thousands a year against roughly $100 for SSL [ycGPHG_ANrE @ 00:10:42]. Tim Lin confirms the governance) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (chain behind those invoices: ATIS is the governance authority, iconectiv is the policy administrator that issues tokens) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (and sets an annual fee based on FCC-filed revenue, and multiple certificate authorities are listed by iconectiv) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm ([3XJ9OkK8aFw @ 00:05:29]. The cheap path small operators reach for is forking the call to a signing provider, which) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (requires a PJSIP patch plus a first and second trunk in FreePBX outbound routes, a setup Chris calls a bubble gum and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (Band-Aid solution [ycGPHG_ANrE @ 00:12:53]. The proper path Tony describes is a real SBC build with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (redundancy, geographic failover on both coasts, DID, credential, and IP mapping, and 911 caller-ID logic. Against that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (cost stack, Crosstalk's resale business peaked at 130,000 to 140,000 calls per month and netted only 15 to 20 percent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (margin every month once profitable, while ClearlyIP handles tens of millions [ycGPHG_ANrE @ 00:07:43].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (Rick at ZCorum turns the RMD rule into a repeatable know-your-customer routine. Verify identity, address, years in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (business, and time at that address, then ask what the service is actually for, because a pizza shop is a different risk from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (a call center or telemarketer [ZLzeR3N0mpc @ 00:07:52]. Terms of service should allow immediate termination on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (reported abuse, the filer certifies full, partial, or no STIR/SHAKEN implementation, and the mitigation plan itself is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (usually just one page long. The sample WOW plan Rick walks through commits to traceback cooperation, vets) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (businesses on name, physical and mailing address, tax ID, phone, email, and PIN, and blocks unassigned numbers, with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (an FCC Registration Number required to file [ZLzeR3N0mpc @ 00:13:22]. Tim Lin layers on the carrier-side) Tj ET
